<tr><td>Answers run to the length limit and stop mid-sentence</td><td>Two distinct mechanisms truncate. Greedy decoding degenerates into repetition — one prompt truncated at 16,384 <em>and</em> at 32,768, and a larger cap does not help. Under the model card's sampler the repetition loop stops, but long reasoning genuinely exhausts the cap: 43 of 198 GPQA Diamond answers exceeded a 30,000-token cap.</td><td>Use the model card's sampler to stop the repetition loop. For genuinely long answers, raise the cap — <a href="#bench">section 8</a> gives the number.</td></tr>
